1
00:00:07,799 --> 00:00:14,245
The thing that finally made Umbrella a state-sized
object was not a weapon, or a virus,

2
00:00:14,265 --> 00:00:18,629
or a secret. It was a purchasing
decision about warehouses.

3
00:00:19,030 --> 00:00:25,939
The United States keeps a strategic national stockpile:
antivirals, antibiotics, ventilators,

4
00:00:25,959 --> 00:00:32,496
protective equipment, all of it distributed across a
dozen unmarked sites and all of it,

5
00:00:32,516 --> 00:00:38,979
by 2030, embarrassingly old. Replacing it was a
nine-billion-dollar programme that four

6
00:00:38,999 --> 00:00:41,139
administrations had deferred.

7
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:48,071
Umbrella bid. Umbrella bid against four consortia, and
Umbrella's bid was not the cheapest

8
00:00:48,091 --> 00:00:52,658
— it was, in fact, forty per cent more
expensive than the next.

9
00:00:53,057 --> 00:00:59,837
It won anyway, in eleven weeks, unanimously,
because of one clause that no competitor

10
00:00:59,857 --> 00:01:05,918
could match and that Catherine Adeyemi had
fought Wesker for six days about.

11
00:01:06,438 --> 00:01:10,711
You are proposing that we hold the stockpile at our
own cost and only invoice when it

12
00:01:10,731 --> 00:01:11,216
is *used*.

13
00:01:11,617 --> 00:01:12,507
Yes.

14
00:01:12,906 --> 00:01:17,691
That is nine billion dollars of inventory financed on
our balance sheet for an event that

15
00:01:17,711 --> 00:01:19,095
may not occur this decade.

16
00:01:19,495 --> 00:01:26,187
It is nine billion dollars that makes it
structurally impossible for this government to

17
00:01:26,207 --> 00:01:32,746
replace us, and that puts an Umbrella logistics
officer in the room for every federal

18
00:01:32,766 --> 00:01:39,381
emergency exercise from now until the end of the
century. Which of those did you think

19
00:01:39,401 --> 00:01:40,385
I was buying?

20
00:01:40,784 --> 00:01:47,775
The European Union followed in March of 2031, with
the same clause. Japan in June. India,

21
00:01:47,795 --> 00:01:50,375
on different terms, in September.

22
00:01:50,775 --> 00:01:57,799
By the autumn of 2031 Umbrella held the medical reserves
of four of the nine largest economies

23
00:01:57,819 --> 00:02:03,345
on earth, at its own expense, and was paid
only when something went wrong.

24
00:02:03,745 --> 00:02:09,887
The narrator wants to underline the shape of this,
because it is the whole of Wesker's

25
00:02:09,907 --> 00:02:11,893
method and it never changed.

26
00:02:12,294 --> 00:02:17,720
He did not take anything. At every stage, for thirty
years, he made himself the answer

27
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:23,167
to a question somebody else was asking, and he made
the answer so much better than the

28
00:02:23,187 --> 00:02:28,613
alternatives that refusing it became the
irresponsible choice. The stockpile was real.

29
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:34,377
The supplies were good. The response times were the
best in the world, and when a hurricane

30
00:02:34,397 --> 00:02:39,760
took out eastern North Carolina in 2031 the
Umbrella trucks were in Greenville before

31
00:02:39,780 --> 00:02:40,963
the National Guard.

32
00:02:41,364 --> 00:02:46,823
Every one of those contracts was a gift. Every one
of them was also a hand closing.

33
00:02:47,973 --> 00:02:56,036
Sovereign-level contract. Four of the two required.
United States, European Union, Japan,

34
00:02:56,056 --> 00:03:04,482
India. One hundred and four thousand personnel, nine
thousand seven hundred of them Absolute.

35
00:03:05,704 --> 00:03:13,420
Tier three. Agency. Umbrella is no longer a company
that governments regulate. It is a

36
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:21,426
company that governments depend upon. Three million
Points. Balance, twenty-seven million

37
00:03:21,446 --> 00:03:29,163
four hundred thousand. The Agency banner is
available. New rarity in pool: Progenitor.

38
00:03:29,752 --> 00:03:31,582
Define the new rarity.

39
00:03:31,983 --> 00:03:39,466
Common improves your company. Rare improves your
capability. Epic improves your reach.

40
00:03:39,486 --> 00:03:42,345
Legendary improves your position.

41
00:03:42,626 --> 00:03:45,283
Progenitor improves *you*.

42
00:03:46,123 --> 00:03:47,433
And the odds?

43
00:03:47,834 --> 00:03:49,781
One in eleven thousand.

44
00:03:50,181 --> 00:03:55,797
The narrator would like to show you what a sovereign
contract looks like from underneath,

45
00:03:55,817 --> 00:03:59,090
because the panels are cold and the
reality was not.

46
00:03:59,491 --> 00:04:05,779
Umbrella's African biosecurity agreement covered nine
countries and cost the company four

47
00:04:05,799 --> 00:04:11,947
billion dollars a year against revenue of
approximately nothing. It placed four hundred

48
00:04:11,967 --> 00:04:18,114
and eleven laboratories, eleven thousand
instruments, and a cold chain that reached, by

49
00:04:18,134 --> 00:04:22,651
2033, ninety-one per cent of the
continent's district hospitals.

50
00:04:23,050 --> 00:04:30,252
A paediatrician in Kisumu named Dr. Achieng Odhiambo,
who had spent nineteen years sending

51
00:04:30,272 --> 00:04:37,474
samples four hundred kilometres by road and waiting
nine days for a result, got a benchtop

52
00:04:37,494 --> 00:04:42,690
box in August of 2031 and a training week
and a service contract.

53
00:04:43,209 --> 00:04:49,086
I want to say something that will sound ungrateful
and is not. For nineteen years I asked

54
00:04:49,106 --> 00:04:54,718
my own government, and four donors, and two
international agencies, for this machine.

55
00:04:54,738 --> 00:04:57,699
I wrote applications. I was
given frameworks.

56
00:04:57,980 --> 00:05:03,071
A company I had never heard of sent me one, and a
woman to teach me to use it, and has

57
00:05:03,091 --> 00:05:08,124
never once asked me for anything, and I do not know
what to do with that, and neither

58
00:05:08,144 --> 00:05:09,610
does anybody I work with.

59
00:05:09,889 --> 00:05:15,070
(very slow) We have a joke here now. When something
arrives that should not have arrived,

60
00:05:15,090 --> 00:05:16,939
we say it fell off the umbrella.

61
00:05:17,339 --> 00:05:25,129
The System's panel for that contract read: *Devotion:
continental. Points: +900,000 recurring.*

62
00:05:25,529 --> 00:05:32,258
Wesker read it in Wilmington and made one note, which
Pell actioned within the week: that

63
00:05:32,278 --> 00:05:38,703
no Umbrella employee in any of the nine countries
was ever to be photographed handing

64
00:05:38,723 --> 00:05:40,219
anything to anybody.

65
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:47,558
The photograph is worth four hundred thousand dollars
in goodwill and it costs the person

66
00:05:47,578 --> 00:05:54,397
in it something that I am not able to give back. We
are not a charity and I will not have

67
00:05:54,417 --> 00:05:55,549
us pose as one.

68
00:05:55,949 --> 00:06:01,825
He pulled twenty times on the Agency banner, at four
hundred thousand Points a ten-pull,

69
00:06:01,845 --> 00:06:05,242
and the narrator will not list two
hundred results.

70
00:06:05,641 --> 00:06:07,362
What matters is four of them.

71
00:06:07,762 --> 00:06:14,121
The first was an Epic: **Cold Chain Sovereign**, a
global refrigerated logistics network

72
00:06:14,141 --> 00:06:20,283
with thirteen hundred vehicles, forty-one aircraft
and its own port facilities, which

73
00:06:20,303 --> 00:06:26,446
arrived on a Tuesday and which the industry press
spent a year describing as the most

74
00:06:26,466 --> 00:06:31,230
impressive piece of operational build-out
in the sector's history.

75
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:38,068
The second was a Rare that he considered, for about
eight seconds, to be the most valuable

76
00:06:38,088 --> 00:06:44,455
thing he had ever pulled: **Multilingual
Competence.** Every language spoken by more than

77
00:06:44,475 --> 00:06:50,697
a million people, complete, permanent, with the
accent of an educated native. He tested

78
00:06:50,717 --> 00:06:54,500
it on the Hungarian night porter at
Arklay, who wept.

79
00:06:55,651 --> 00:06:58,581
Legendary. The Antarctic Facility.

80
00:06:59,800 --> 00:07:06,765
The Antarctic Facility. A subsurface complex of
fourteen levels in interior Antarctica.

81
00:07:06,785 --> 00:07:13,589
B S L four throughout. A cryogenic hall of four
thousand cradles. Dedicated power, an

82
00:07:13,609 --> 00:07:20,654
airstrip, and a deep-water port three hundred and
forty kilometres away. Six hundred and

83
00:07:20,674 --> 00:07:27,478
eleven Absolute personnel. A Tyrant cohort of
eight, cradled. Jurisdiction: none. The

84
00:07:27,498 --> 00:07:34,382
Antarctic Treaty forbids military activity and
mineral extraction. It does not mention

85
00:07:34,402 --> 00:07:35,105
research.

86
00:07:35,694 --> 00:07:40,718
He read the last line of that panel and laughed —
the second time, and the last.

87
00:07:41,117 --> 00:07:45,478
And then, on the nineteenth pull of the
twentieth ten, the room went black.

88
00:07:47,177 --> 00:07:54,439
Progenitor. Origin. One sealed ampoule. Contents:
the first strain. Not a weapon. Not

89
00:07:54,459 --> 00:08:01,977
a cure. The thing all of it came from. The effect on
the host is permanent, irreversible

90
00:08:01,997 --> 00:08:10,115
and categorical. Requirement: Viral Affinity forty. Your
current Viral Affinity is twenty-four.

91
00:08:10,135 --> 00:08:16,455
Do not open this early. I will not be able to
stop what happens if you do.

92
00:08:17,704 --> 00:08:23,360
The narrator would like you to understand that in four
and a half years, across two hundred

93
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:27,974
thousand words of panels, that is the first
time the System ever said *I*.

94
00:08:28,495 --> 00:08:30,685
(very cold) Say that again.

95
00:08:31,084 --> 00:08:32,876
Viral Affinity forty.

96
00:08:33,277 --> 00:08:34,927
The last sentence.

97
00:08:35,657 --> 00:08:37,482
Do not open this early.

98
00:08:37,881 --> 00:08:44,303
You said *I will not be able to stop what happens*.
You have never used that word about

99
00:08:44,323 --> 00:08:49,411
